Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for swat-or-buy project

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1 as a production dependency
- Used npm (the project's package manager) to install the package

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `src/main.ts`:
- Added import statement: `import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';`
- Called `inject()` function at the top of the application entry point
- This ensures analytics tracking is initialized before any other application code runs

### 3. Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
- `src/main.ts` - Added analytics import and initialization

## Implementation Details
This is a vanilla TypeScript/Vite project (no React framework). According to the Vercel Analytics documentation, for non-React applications, the `inject()` function from `@vercel/analytics` should be used to initialize analytics tracking. This was added at the very top of the main.ts entry point to ensure it runs before any other application code.

## Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ All 8 tests pass without issues
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
- ✅ Lock files properly updated

## Notes
The analytics will begin tracking page views and web vitals once the application is deployed to Vercel. No additional configuration is needed for basic analytics tracking. The analytics can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab for this project.
